  "full_text": "So, you know, they talk about stuff being above your pay grade, right? I just thought of something that's appropriate for my job. You know, I was talking to the Queen of England and I said, hey, maybe you need to make your people poor so that they make rock music. God said that boredom causes craftiness. Boredom causes craftiness. So like our world, one of the characteristics of our particular decade is very busyness. Now we have these phones all over and we're busy, busy, busy, busy. Boredom causes craftiness. So it is within the power of the king to try and alter the busyness of people. Well technically a kink of bad phones or some shit like that or do something about the the cluttered You know or all the people You know what if something drastically has to be done about the the way we live our lives nah like You know there was a time when people were country farm farm boys And just think of the contrast between a farm boy in the 1930s and today's people. Think of the contrast. Now, what about God? God likes it when his works are glorified, not man's works. And, of course, he probably gets bored from century to century. He probably wants it to change, not stay the same. Yeah, you can roll one if you want. Can I have some tobacco? What? Can I have a little bit? Yeah, you can have some, yeah. So, people on the streets are the other extreme. They're totally bored. But other people have busy, busy lives with their cell phones and shit all the time. I think there's a problem with too much busyness. And I don't know if everything is... I don't know if something's rotten in the state of Denmark. That's not the right expression. But God wants his works glorified. So the question is, are the citizens reaching their potential?",
